~ mean
Shopkeeper: That's... simply not true.  
Shopkeeper: Hells, he's a kid. You barely met him. 
Shopkeeper: And how would you know what's best for my Sarah? You just got here. 
- Okay. Sorry. 
	Shopkeeper: Just... be nice, yeah? He's like a son to me.[do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", -1)] => next
- Whatever. 
	Shopkeeper: ... => next2
- Fuck him. And fuck Sarah, too. 
	Shopkeeper: ... [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", 1)][do Variables.set_var("1_3_death", 1)][wait=1.5][do DialogueFuncs.force_next_interaction()] => END 

~ nice
Shopkeeper: Oh, she's an angel. 
Shopkeeper: She's all I have. Everything I do, I do for her. 
- So is she, like, part of your little cult? [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 1]
	Shopkeeper: I'd be careful throwing that word around, if I were you. 
	Shopkeeper: People here prefer "church".
	Shopkeeper: But yes. Of course she is. 
	Shopkeeper: Not a full member yet, though. She's too young. You can only become one once you're sixteen. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)]
	- Good. => next
	- Is that what she wants?
		Shopkeeper: It's what's right. 
		Shopkeeper: And what's needed. 
		- If you say so. => next
		- Sounds more like it's what's needed, rather than what's right.
			Shopkeeper: It's both. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)]
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]...
			Shopkeeper: You're new here. You seem smart. 
			Shopkeeper: So be careful with what you say and who you say it to. 
			Shopkeeper: Not everyone is as understanding and open-minded as I am.
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]And don't take it as a threat, but as soon as I feel like your words or doubts might put Sarah in danger, I'll stop being understanding and open minded, too. 
			Shopkeeper: I hope you can understand. 
			- I do. I'll be careful. 
				Shopkeeper: Good. => next
			- I'm not doubting anything. I'm just asking a question. 
				Shopkeeper: Which I answered truthfully. 
				Shopkeeper: And those two can very often be the same thing, at the end of the day. => next
			- Just want to make sure you're not brainwashing the child. 
				Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]I can only hope your attitude will change, once you feel the Goddess's warmth. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)]
				Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]If not, may She have mercy and help you find the light, for I won't. I can't. => next2
- She a true believer? [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >= 0]
	Shopkeeper: Course she is. 
	Shopkeeper: I've been teaching her the ways of our Goddess ever since she was born. 
	Shopkeeper: She's not a full member yet, though. She's too young. Can only become one once she's sixteen. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", -1)]
	- Good. => next 
	- Is that what she wants?
		Shopkeeper: It's what's right. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]And what's needed. 
		- It sure is. => next
		- She should only do it if she really wants to.
			Shopkeeper: That's... not exactly how things work around here. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)]
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]...
			Shopkeeper: You're new here. You seem smart. 
			Shopkeeper: So be careful with what you say and who you say it to. 
			Shopkeeper: Not everyone is as understanding and open minded as I am.
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]And don't take it as a threat, but as soon as I feel like your words or doubts might put Sarah in danger, I'll stop being understanding and open minded, too. 
			Shopkeeper: I hope you can understand. 
			- I do. I'll be careful. 
				Shopkeeper: Good. => next
			- I'm not doubting anything. I'm just asking a question. 
				Shopkeeper: Which I answered truthfully. 
				Shopkeeper: And those two can very often be the same thing, at the end of the day. => next 
			- Just wanted to make sure her faith is genuine. 
				Shopkeeper: It is.[do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", -1)]
				Shopkeeper: Not that it's any of your business. 
				Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Tread carefully. I'd do literally anything to protect her.
				Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]I mean it. => next2
- You two don't look that much alike. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]...Yeah. She gets her looks from her mother. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=laugh]Thankfully. 
	- Don't sell yourself short. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=laugh]Hah. Flattery does work on me, can't lie.[do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", 1)] => next
	- What happened to her?
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Don't really wanna talk about it, if you don't mind. 
		- Of course. I understand.
			Shopkeeper: Appreciate it.[do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", 1)] => next
		- And why not?
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]I think that's my business and mine only. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]And I'd appreciate it if you didn't pry further. 
			- Okay. Sorry. 
				Shopkeeper: Don't worry about it. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", -1)] => next
			- Fine. => next2
- She's lucky to have you. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=laugh]Hah, nowhere near as lucky as I am to have her.
	Shopkeeper: But thank you. I often wonder if I'm doing right by her. 
	Shopkeeper: Goddess knows I've tried my best, and then some. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]But it's... hard. A child shouldn't have to grow up in a world like this. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]I'm not doubting the Goddess's work, of course. Just wish things could have been different.
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]For Sarah's sake. 
	- I understand. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Means a lot. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", 1)] => next
	- I'm sure she appreciates it. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]She's too kind not to. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", 1)] => next
	- That comes dangerously close to blasphemy. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >= -1]
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]... [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", -1)]
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]You're right. Forgive me. => next
	

~ next
Shopkeeper: Anyway, I've got some errands to run. I'll leave you to it. 
Shopkeeper: Pretty small batch today, and it's the best way to learn, if you ask me. 
Shopkeeper: Oh, almost forgot! I also have this old, infected gramophone just lying around. I've been meaning to cleanse it forever but I haven't found the time.
Shopkeeper: It might just be broken, but you should try cleansing it first, see if it helps. Would be nice for Sarah to be able to listen to some music again. 
Shopkeeper: Think you're up to it?
- Sure am. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=laugh]That's the spirit! [do DialogueFuncs.add_object_to_workbench("gramophone")]
	Shopkeeper: Might be late by the time I get back, so feel free to go to bed once you're done. 
	Shopkeeper: See you tomorrow morning. 
	- See you then.
		Shopkeeper: Good luck.[do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_close")] => END 
	- Actually, I have some questions I've been meaning to ask. 
		Shopkeeper: Oh. Okay. Shoot. => questions 
- Think I've had enough for one day. 
	Shopkeeper: No worries. I understand. [do Variables.set_var("gramophone", false)]
	Shopkeeper: See you tomorrow morning. Good luck.
	- See you then.
		Shopkeeper: Good luck.[do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_close")] => END  
	- Actually, I have some questions I've been meaning to ask. 
		Shopkeeper: Oh. Okay. Shoot. => questions 
		
~ next2
Shopkeeper: Anyway, I've got some errands to run. I'll leave you to it. [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", 2)]
Shopkeeper: Might be late by the time I get back. See you tomorrow morning. [do Variables.set_var("gramophone", false)]
- See you.
	Shopkeeper: [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_slam")]... => END
- Actually, I have some questions I've been meaning to ask...
	Shopkeeper: I don't feel like talking right now. Some other time.
	Shopkeeper: [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_slam")]... => END 
	
~ questions
Shopkeeper: ... 
- Were you waiting for me last night? Didn't even get to properly knock before you opened the door. [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "wait") == false]
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Oh, well, uh, kind of. I'm sorry if that was weird. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "wait", true)]
	Shopkeeper: Been working alone for a long time. Hasn't been ideal, but I got used to it. Forgot how to behave around people, seems like. 
	Shopkeeper: It's just that I've known for a while someone bearing the Gift would come, and yesterday I felt this urge to look out the window right before you came into view.
	Shopkeeper: And there you were. As soon as I saw you, I somehow knew it was you. Can't explain it any more than that, though I wish I could.
	Shopkeeper: Plus, I didn't want your knocking to wake Sarah up, truth be told. She's a light sleeper. 
	- To be honest, I, myself, kind of knew this was your house even before Joan pointed it to me.
		Shopkeeper: There you have it. The Goddess works in ways unknown to us. => questions
	- No harm, no foul.
		Shopkeeper: Appreciate it. => questions
	- Err, not sure how I feel about that. 
		Shopkeeper: I know, I'm being odd again. But it's the truth. => questions
- How do you know so much about me already? [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "know") == false]
	Shopkeeper: Your arrival was heralded by the Elders. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "know", true)]
	Shopkeeper: They told me someone bearing the Gift would soon come to help me around with the shop. Goddess knows I could use it.
	Shopkeeper: To be completely honest, though, you never know with them. Their predictions have been wrong just as often as they've been right.
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]...Make sure not to tell anyone I said that, please. 
	Shopkeeper: I've got my own connection with the Goddess, though. She told me what I needed to know Herself.
	- She talked to me, too. In my sleep, in what felt like a dream. Told me to come here. 
		Shopkeeper: I'm well aware. She rarely does that, you know. 
		- Any idea why She chose me?
			Shopkeeper: None. She's not exactly straightforward, our Goddess. Gods rarely are.
			Shopkeeper: All I know is you're important to her, and She wants me to train you. 
			Shopkeeper: And that's all I need to know for now. => questions
		- Interesting. => questions
	- I see. => questions
- Have there really been no deaths caused by the Cullings here? [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "unaffected") == false]
	Shopkeeper: Sure haven't. Not a single one, ever since they started all those years ago. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "unaffected", true)]
	Shopkeeper: The sky does turn red in the morning, heralding a Culling day, and we've had people die just outside our walls. 
	Shopkeeper: Gruesome, horrific way to go. Glad I've only witnessed it this one time.
	Shopkeeper: But inside, nothing. Not once. The Goddess cares for and protects us.
	- How is this possible?
		Shopkeeper: You'll have to see it to believe it. Perhaps, if you're a doubter now, those doubts will vanish then. 
		Shopkeeper: Like I said, the Cullings are punishment for humanity's sins over the years. And a way to cleanse the Earth and start anew.
		Shopkeeper: We, however, have nothing to be punished for. We've been loyal to our Goddess, unlike most of the outside sinners. Their deaths are necessary. As are our lives. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Sounds brutal, I know. But they've been ruthless to our planet, our home, driving it to a point where it was nearly uninhabitable anymore. 
		Shopkeeper: Something had to be done. 
		- I've seen countless people die horrible deaths. I can tell you, it is not worth it. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Who are we to say, at the end of the day? It's how things are now and we have to adjust to it, either way.[do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)] => questions
		- They had it coming. Hopefully some good comes out of it. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Time will tell. Either way, it's how things are now.[do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", -1)] => questions
	- That's... incredible. 
		Shopkeeper: Sure is. We're truly blessed. => questions
- Who are these "Elders"? [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "elders") == false]
	Shopkeeper: They're the founders and leaders of our wonderful village and church. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "elders", true)]
	Shopkeeper: They're the only ones here who can communicate directly with the Goddess, besides me, of course. 
	Shopkeeper: They're very old, hence the name. They rarely come out of their home. They have underlings and messengers in their service, and that's how they usually communicate the Goddess's will and teachings to the rest of us.
	Shopkeeper: There's a chance you won't ever see them yourself, but it's safer to assume they're aware of your every move. 
	Shopkeeper: They don't take kindly to meddling newcomers. And they're not known for being forgiving to heretics and blasphemers. 
	Shopkeeper: Since you're not technically part of our church yet, the most severe form of punishment you could undergo is exile. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]But once you have taken the oath and become a fully fledged member, the punishment for sinning is either flogging, or death, depending on the severity of your actions. 
	Shopkeeper: Sounds worse than it is. All you have to do is not speak against or openly defy our Goddess. 
	- Sounds simple enough.
		Shopkeeper: It is. => questions
	- That's... fucked up. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Salvation comes at a cost.[do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)][do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)] => questions
- Kind of feels like I'm joining a cult. [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "cult") == false && Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 1]
	Shopkeeper: Eh, people here are just like everywhere else. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)][do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "cult", true)]
	Shopkeeper: Some good apples, some bad ones. Perhaps a few rotten ones here and there. 
	Shopkeeper: There are some practices and beliefs which might seem... odd, especially to an outsider.
	Shopkeeper: Way I see it, at least we've got a purpose.
	Shopkeeper: Goes a long way, what with the state of the world right now and everything.
	- Guess I can respect that. 
		Shopkeeper: Just keep an open mind, yeah? => questions
	- Still feels weird. 
		Shopkeeper: I get it. I do. Just give it a bit of time. Besides, you've got me to help you settle in.[do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)] => questions
- What was your daughter talking about last night, about the dreams and everything? [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "dream") == false]
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]That's... complicated. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "dream", true)]
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]She used to have nightmares every night a while back. It was a hard time for her. For us. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Then they just... stopped.
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Looks like they're a thing again. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Her abundant imagination should be a source of joy, especially at her age. 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]It's been anything but. 
	- I'm sorry to hear that. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Yeah. Appreciate it. => questions
	- What does she dream about?
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]It's... difficult to explain. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]She likes to draw what she remembers in the morning.
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Don't freak out if you see such drawings around the house. 
		- Noted. => questions
		- I'll... try. => questions 
	- She said they're back and unhappy. Who's "they"?
		Shopkeeper: She sees... creatures. Animals, and stuff. They talk to her. 
		Shopkeeper: Some of them are friendly. Others, not so much. 
		Shopkeeper: She doesn't go into too much detail, you know? And I don't like to push her. 
		- Makes sense. => questions 
		- Perhaps it would help her to see someone. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=laugh]Like a shrink, you mean? Hah. You'll find no such thing here. => questions
- So, do you people sacrifice humans and stuff? [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "sacrifice") == false and Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "questions") >= 3] 
	Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Uh, no, course not. [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "sacrifice", true)]
	- Okay. => questions
	- You sure?
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Sure I'm sure. No sacrifices here. None. 
		- Okay then. => questions
		- Kind of sounds like you're lying to me.
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Look, there are some things you'll only get to know once you become a full member of the church. [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "sacrifice_lie", true)]
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]But trust me, we don't sacrifice anyone in the... traditional sense, and never involuntarily. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]That's all I can say for now. I could get in trouble for saying more, so please, drop it for now. 
			- Okay, I trust you. => questions
			- Fine. For now. => questions
- I think your Goddess brainwashed me. [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "brainwashed") == false]
	Shopkeeper: That can't be right. She wouldn't. [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "brainwashed", true)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "brainwash", 1)]
	Shopkeeper: What makes you say that?
	- Nevermind. Forget it. 
		Shopkeeper: If you so wish. 
		Shopkeeper: Just trust me, I know what I'm talking about. She would never. => questions
	- I can't remember anything that happened before She visited me. 
		Shopkeeper: Look, perhaps you were in... an accident, or something. Hit your head, or got run over by a car, or the like. Lost your memories. These things happen. 
		Shopkeeper: The Goddess looks out for those in need. For those who are lost. Suffering. 
		Shopkeeper: Think about it. It makes much more sense than Her "brainwashing" you. 
		- I guess that's a possibility. 
			Shopkeeper: The past is the past. Perhaps you'd be dead if it wasn't for Her. 
			Shopkeeper: I'm sure I would...
			Shopkeeper: You've been given a second chance. Cherish it. Embrace it.
			Shopkeeper: Life is worth living. Especially as part of Her family. => questions
		- I really don't think that's the case. 
			Shopkeeper: Look, give it some time. Think about it. Do some soul-searching. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)][do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)]
			Shopkeeper: I'm sure the answers lie in there, somewhere.
			Shopkeeper: But you've been given a second chance. Don't take it for granted. => questions
- What's up with the tree branches and the candles? [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "candles") == false]
	Shopkeeper: What do you mean? [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "candles", true)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "questions", 1)]
	Shopkeeper: Oh. It must be the Goddess's way of helping you out. Of showing you how much more your body can take. 
	Shopkeeper: And also to, uh, remind you that She's always watching.
	Shopkeeper: They're not really there, though. They're in your head. I, myself, see spider webs and bugs. Cool, eh? => questions
- (MOVE ON) That's it, for now. [if Variables.get_char_var("NPC_4", "questions") >= 1]
	Shopkeeper: Alright then. I'm heading out. 
	- Thanks for clearing things up. 
		Shopkeeper: Of course. Good luck. [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_close")] => END
	- See you tomorrow. 
		Shopkeeper: Good luck. [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_close")] => END

=> END

